The original default-constructs `values` and `stringIndexes` and then copy-assigns into them. This version copy-constructs them directly in the member initializer list, which skips the default construction and the assignment step.

Both members end up with the same contents as before, and every other member is default-initialized exactly as in the original. Behavior is therefore unchanged.

```cpp
FieldBase::FieldBase(const FieldBase &field)
    : values(field.values),
      stringIndexes(field.stringIndexes)
{
}
```